      "artist": "Ilka Nghinamupika",
      "description": "This image shows the Bushman people busy harvesting the deadly Bushman's hunting poison. In the vast expanse of Namibia's Tsumkwe village_Otjozondjupa region, Bushman people engage in the ancient art of harvesting Adenium boehmianum, known colloquially as the \"bushman's poison.\" With practiced hands, they carefully gather these potent plants, essential to their traditional hunting techniques and cultural heritage. Amidst the arid landscape, this ritual embodies a timeless connection between the Bushman people and the land, preserving centuries-old wisdom and customs.",
